Q: Click after hover effect
A: <p><a href="https://jsfiddle.net/kmdyuwt8/2/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://jsfiddle.net/kmdyuwt8/2/</a></p>
<p>You need to add an open class</p>
<pre class="lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>.wrapper #menu.show {
  width: 300px;
  height: 100%;
  transition: width 1s linear;
}
</code></pre>
<p>And toggle it on hover.</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>let elm = document.querySelector('.hamburger');
function toggleMenu() {
  document.querySelector('#menu').classList.toggle('show');
}
elm.onmouseenter = toggleMenu;
elm.onmouseleave = toggleMenu;
</code></pre>
